 Schlafli: (p-2)(q-2) < 4: [(3, 3), (3, 4), (3, 5), (4, 3), (5, 3)] (5); = 4: [(3, 6), (4, 4), (6, 3)] (3)
 PSL(2,2)         order    6 on  3 points (formula    6); sympy: is_alternating=False is_symmetric=True
 PSL(2,3)         order   12 on  4 points (formula   12); sympy: is_alternating=True is_symmetric=False
 PGL(2,3)         order   24 on  4 points (formula   24); sympy: is_alternating=False is_symmetric=True
 PSL(2,4)=SL(2,4) order   60 on  5 points (formula   60); sympy: is_alternating=True is_symmetric=False
 PSL(2,5)         order   60 on  6 points (formula   60); sympy: is_alternating=False is_symmetric=False; involutions 15, Klein four-subgroups 5, conjugation action on them: kernel 1, image order 60, image is A_5: True; point stabilizer order 10 (D_10), transitive on 6 points: True
 PSL(2,7)         order  168 on  8 points (formula  168); sympy: is_alternating=False is_symmetric=False
 PSL(2,17)        order 2448 on 18 points (formula 2448)
 orders 6, 12, 24, 60, 60, 168, 2448 confirmed; finite rotation groups of R^3 have orders n, 2n, 12, 24, 60 (Klein), so PSL(2,7) and PSL(2,17) are not among them

